  "dashboard": {
    "autoRerun": true,
    "cards": [
      {
        "id": "t",
        "kind": "text",
        "size": "2x1",
        "title": "Two 7-DOF SRS arms on one object",
        "options": {
          "markdown": true,
          "text": "**Redundancy.** A rigid grasp fixes the full pose of each hand (3 position + 3 orientation), so two hands on one object give **12 constraints**. Two 7-DOF arms have **14 joints: 2 left over**, one self-motion per arm (the elbow swings about the shoulder-wrist line while the hand stays put). Two 6-DOF arms (J5 locked) have **12 joints for 12 constraints: no slack**, so the object pose fixes both postures, the elbow bias does nothing, and at the default pose the arms run into J3 and J6 limits and miss the grasp by about 3.5 mm and 3.3 deg."
        }
      },
